# VitranShop Core

## Product
- Kotlin **Compose Multiplatform** app (Android, iOS, Web, Desktop).
- Shared UI and logic live in `shared/` (`commonMain`).
- Persian (fa-IR), **RTL** by default.
- No purchase flow yet: no Cart, Checkout, Payment, or Place order.
- Screen map: `docs/ui-reference/screens.md`.

## UI workflow (important)
- Shopper screens: screenshots in `docs/ui-reference/` plus **live shop.app** are the source of truth for **colors, spacing, shapes, and section patterns**.
- **Mandatory live inspection (shopper):** Before implementing or refining shopper UI, open the **matching shop.app URL/section** in the agent browser and inspect that exact block. Do not guess from memory or screenshots alone.
- **Merchant admin:** `docs/ui-reference/admin/` (Shopify Admin screenshots + store-plan) is the source of truth. Do **not** open shop.app for admin pages such as Create store (`/admin/stores/new`), Store plan (`/admin/stores/plan`), Upgrade plan (`/admin/stores/plan/upgrade`), Manage plans (`/admin/plans`), Add product (`/admin/products/new`), or Select category (`/admin/categories/new`).
- **About Us:** `docs/ui-reference/about/` is the source of truth for `/about` (`AboutScreen`). Do **not** open shop.app for this marketing page.
- **Auth register card:** `docs/ui-reference/auth/` (Shopify signup-style). Login `/account/login` (mobile+password); register `/account/register` then OTP at `/account/register/verify`. Forgot `/account/forgot` (mobile + send code) then reset `/account/forgot/reset` (OTP + new password, no confirm).
- **Account / Profile:** `docs/ui-reference/account/` (shop.app account hub + profile). Live shop.app `/account` is sign-in gated; use screenshots plus re-check when a session is available. Hub `/account`, edit profile `/account/profile`, referrals `/account/referrals`, following `/account/following`, settings `/account/settings`, my stores `/account/stores`, users `/account/users`, user detail `/account/users/{id}`, cities `/account/cities`, city detail `/account/cities/{id}`, add city `/account/cities/new`. Merchant-with-store opens plan dashboard from the hub.
- User screenshots complement live inspection for shopper UI; they do **not** replace it.
- Do **not** mark a shopper section done until you have opened shop.app for that section and reflected what you measured.
- Build UI **piece by piece** (one component or one section per task).
- Do **not** implement an entire screen unless the user explicitly asks for that assembly step.
- New shopper sections: always verify **responsive sizing** and the **gap above** the previous section on live shop.app — see rule `page-section-workflow.mdc`.

## Phase
- Current phase: **UI + mock data only**. No real API calls from screens until a section is explicitly wired.
- Prefer fake/local data so screens look complete.
- Never ship PDP placeholders like title `محصول`, merchant `فروشگاه`, price `—`, or “description coming soon” — use realistic fake copy.

## API contract
- Source of truth: `docs/postman/vitran-api.postman_collection.json` (131 requests, 128 `/api/v1` business routes). Summary: `docs/api-contract.md`.
- `category_slug` / `category_slugs` are taxonomy **strings** (example `aa-1-2`). Keep the flexible serializer for legacy numbers; do not invent numeric category ids.
- Product cards use `main_image.url` (or `images[]` where `is_main` is true). Do not assume `images[0]` is the cover.
- Shop collections: public `GET /shops/{id}/collections` feeds `StoreScreen` tiles. Seller create/update/delete lives on the store edit screen. Collection rows have `product_count` and no cover image. Do not add a second collection model.
- Seller shop create/update sends SEO, rules, shipping methods, working hours, fulfillment type, webhook, and socials (`bale`, `rubika`, `tiktok`) from the create-store and edit-store forms. On edit, omit a profile field the user did not change — shop GET may still leave those fields out.

## Language
- Code, comments, and Cursor rules/skills: **English**.
- User-facing strings: **Persian**.

## When to use
- Always. Applies to every chat in this repo.

## When to update
- Product decisions change (e.g. purchase flow returns, new platforms, locale rules).
- Screen map or phase (mock → API) changes.
- You keep re-explaining the same core constraint to the agent.
